{
  "id": "quantal-hypothesis",
  "term": "quantal hypothesis",
  "definition": "The quantal hypothesis is the idea that communication at a chemical synapse occurs in discrete units, with neurotransmitter released from individual synaptic vesicles. In this view, each vesicle carries a roughly uniform packet, or quantum, whose release produces a postsynaptic response, although the size of that response can also vary with postsynaptic receptors and presynaptic influences on vesicle content.",
